    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI've read through the documentation, unsure if I have missed something.\r\n\r\nWhen I was using telescope, I had something like this in my config:\r\n```\r\ntelescope().live_grep({default_text=vim.fn.expand(\"<cword>\")})\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs something similar possible with mini.pick? (I probably should be using some LSP to find all references, but sometimes it's still useful..)",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've read through the documentation, unsure if I have missed something.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I was using telescope, I had something like this in my config:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"telescope().live_grep({default_text=vim.fn.expand(&quot;&lt;cword&gt;&quot;)})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">telescope().live_grep({default_text=vim.fn.expand(\"&lt;cword&gt;\")})\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is something similar possible with mini.pick? (I probably should be using some LSP to find all references, but sometimes it's still useful..)</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nI've read through the documentation, unsure if I have missed something.\nWhen I was using telescope, I had something like this in my config:\ntelescope().live_grep({default_text=vim.fn.expand(\"<cword>\")})\n\nIs something similar possible with mini.pick? (I probably should be using some LSP to find all references, but sometimes it's still useful..)",
